  {
    "id": "why",
    "title": "Ideals that breed masters",
    "labels": [
      "Antinomies",
      "Hidden nobility",
      "Who equalises"
    ],
    "lines": [
      "Confiscate every fortune, and someone still decides who gets a home and who may leave.",
      "We Manufacture Our Own Masters calls these traps antinomies, and finds them in every camp.",
      "The author knew them from communism, where levelled incomes still hid a nobility without titles."
    ],
    "emotionalPlan": {
      "arc": "A concrete provocation rises into a named problem, then grounds itself in personal history.",
